C port of the v0 demangler features that upstream added to src/v0.rs only:
pattern types (`W<type><pat>`, rust-lang/rustc-demangle#81) and splatted fn
arguments (`w` before a type, printed as `#[rustc_splat] `, #90 and #93). The
C demangler printed such symbols undemangled while rustc_demangle demangles
them, so the native_c differential fuzz target failed its assert_eq on e.g.
`_RINvC5krate3fooWmRm1_m9_E`. The smoke_test cases added here fail without
the demangle.c change.

The legacy `$u..$` hunk mirrors the lowercase-hex check in src/legacy.rs. It
does not change behaviour: try_parse_uint already rejects anything but
lowercase hex digits.

Upstream: none found; crates/native-c at upstream HEAD (4023665) lacks both.

